      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Already did a good job documenting what APIs are cancelation points and what are not, but could do better, and have some review of this.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "And - especailly unclear on a few socket ones - shoudl review more carefully (like write/send).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "And semantics we want for InputStream - all reads always cancalation points? Thats a big constraint!",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Consider if there is any point in a more lightweight version of cancelation point that MAY cancel - but without the primise. I dont think thats useful.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
